--============================================================
-- OLD CHROME 2024
-- EXECUTOR SCRIPT
--============================================================
--
-- Recreates the 2024 Roblox "Chrome" top bar (the unibar) from a
-- snapshot of the real TopBarApp. The snapshot matches client
-- 0.638 (August 2024): its icon atlases are UIBlox img_set_1x_7
-- (rbxassetid://109435167893110) and img_set_1x_8
-- (rbxassetid://97484125241209).
--
-- Every behaviour below is taken from the 2024 CoreScripts
-- (Modules/Chrome) rather than approximated:
--
--   * Opening / closing the unibar uses the 2024 150 ms spring.
--     Icons slide out from behind the toggle while the pill grows,
--     and the toggle's cube morphs into an X.
--   * Highlighter  = hover with a mouse, or press on touch.
--     SelectedHighlighter = nine_dot while its submenu is open.
--     Selected integrations show their "On" icon instead.
--   * The submenu closes on any mouse release or tap that is not
--     on one of its buttons, and stays open while pinning.
--   * Most-recently-used slots: 4 on desktop, 2 on a phone in
--     landscape, 1 in portrait, 0 in tiny portrait. This is what
--     keeps the open bar on screen on phones.
--   * The health bar sits under the open pill, or beside the
--     closed one, whenever the character is hurt.
--   * Submenu labels match 2024 ("Inventory", not "Backpack").
--
-- NATIVE COREUI
--
--   Chat, PlayerList, Backpack, Emotes and the Escape menu are the
--   real Roblox ones. Buttons call the same native objects the 2024
--   integrations called (PlayerList controller, BackpackScript,
--   SettingsHub) when the executor provides getgc. Otherwise they use
--   the disabled native top bar's own buttons, or call the native key
--   handler directly.
--
--   Synthetic key presses (Tab / Backquote / Escape) are only sent to
--   keyboard-and-mouse players. On touch, one fake key press switches
--   Roblox to keyboard mode: a cursor appears and the thumbstick and
--   jump button disappear until the next touch.
--
-- PHONES AND TABLETS
--
--   Roblox's own menu button sits, invisible, on top of the 2024
--   Roblox icon, so a tap on the icon is a real tap on Roblox's
--   button: the menu opens at once and the device stays in touch
--   mode. Without it, the button is pressed for you. The cursor is kept
--   hidden. Game scripts (the thumbstick / jump button, game UI) always
--   read PreferredInput as Touch, so a stray keyboard or mouse event
--   never switches them to the PC layout, and Roblox's own UI is put
--   back in touch mode once no finger is on the screen. Nothing ever
--   covers the screen while a finger is down (a held jump button would
--   stay stuck).
--
--   Nothing pops up: status goes to the console and to
--   getgenv().OldChrome2024Status.
--
--   Icon states are read back from the native UI (event driven,
--   with a light 4 Hz poll as a safety net), so the native hotkeys
--   / Tab ` . and the native menus always stay in sync.
--
-- OPTIONAL ORDER (open unibar):
--
--   chrome_toggle, nine_dot, backpack, emotes, chat, leaderboard,
--   DIV1, trust_and_safety
--
--   Backpack always comes before Emotes. Which of backpack / emotes
--   / chat / leaderboard are in the bar follows the 2024 rules:
--   most recently used from the submenu, plus anything pinned.
--
-- Re-executing replaces the previous copy cleanly (its signal
-- connections are disconnected too).
-- getgenv().OldChrome2024Unload() restores the native top bar.
--
-- Run on its own, it loads the whole 2024 GUI (bloxy-paradox/2024-gui.lua):
-- the 2023 new GUI's fast flags, a rejoin so they take effect, then this
-- top bar and the 2023 new chat. FullGui = false loads only the top bar.
--
-- Settings can be overridden before executing:
--   getgenv().OldChrome2024Config = { ClosePanelsOnStart = false }
--   (HideCursorOnTouch / KeepTouchMode / SpoofTouchInput = false for
--   a tablet used with a real mouse or keyboard)
--
--============================================================

